{
  "reference_answer": "Yeah, I'd say I do, but with a bit of a caveat. What I really like about big cities is the sheer convenience — you've got transport running late into the night, food from pretty much anywhere in the world, and there's always something on, whether it's a gig or a gallery. That said, I couldn't live right in the centre. The noise and the crowds wear me down after a while, so I'd rather be somewhere on the edge where I can dip in when I want and then retreat when I've had enough. So it's not really the city itself I love — it's having the option to be part of it without being swallowed up by it.",
